    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d63">

                <pb facs="0128" n="48" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg48"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Pekin, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-02-27"><hi rendition="#italic">February 27,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 551.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm on the overleaf
                    my telegram<anchor n="a" xml:id="d63-f1"/> of the 26th instant and Department’s
                        reply<anchor n="a" xml:id="d63-f2"/> of to-day with reference to former
                    United States concession at Tientsin.</p>
                <pb facs="0129" n="49" xml:id="pg49"/>
                <p>I inclose copy of my correspondence with Consul Ragsdale and General Chaffee
                    which fully explains the necessity for the action I deemed proper to take in the
                    matter.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>









